${_CLR_BOLD}COMMANDS${_CLR_RESET}

${_CLR_BOLD_CYAN}help${_CLR_RESET}
	Show this help.

${_CLR_BOLD_CYAN}cache show|list|delete${_CLR_RESET}  [dir-spec] [--name <pattern>]
	Manage Actions caches.
	--name <pattern>   Only affect caches whose key matches the glob
					(e.g. --name '*ccache*' or --name 'sccache-Windows-*')

${_CLR_BOLD_CYAN}ci stop|start|restart|status${_CLR_RESET}  [dir-spec] [--failed]
	Manage workflow runs.
	--failed   Only re-run failed/cancelled/timed_out runs

${_CLR_BOLD_CYAN}submodules init|deinit|update|list|details${_CLR_RESET}  [dir-spec] [--confirm] [--latest] [--all] [--module …] [--tag …]
	Submodule operations (update walks ROOT in dependency order).
	init     git submodule update --init --recursive
	deinit   git submodule deinit --all -f
	list     name, path and URL from .gitmodules (or "none").
	details  First-level only (not list). Columns: NAME, URL, PIN, LATEST.
			LATEST is the newest recognised release in the module
			(same criterion as update --latest). A (semver) suffix is
			added only when the ref text is not already that semver.
			Read-only. --all lists tags on master/main and origin branches.
			--module <name|path>     only that first-level module
			--module '!a+!b'         all first-level modules except those
	update   First-level modules only; nested ones stay on the SHAs
			recorded by their parent after the roots are staged.
			--module / --module '!…' as in details.
			Rows not selected still appear in the plan as No changes.
			--tag <tag>  requires a positive --module. That row pins the
			exact tag (character match) and ignores family / --latest.
			DRY_RUN=1 prints the plan and does not checkout.

			Policy (branch= in .gitmodules of the parent):
			A  branch=master
				Float to origin/master. Already at that SHA → No changes.
			B1 no master, checkout is a recognised release tag
				Move to the latest tag in the same family.
			B2 no master, checkout is not a tag
				Pin to the latest tag of the inferred family (downgrade OK).
				Else the newest recognised release.
			--latest  B1 and B2 use the newest recognised release in the
			module, including a new major. Ignored on a --tag row.
			Unrecognised pins → UNRESOLVED. --confirm / non-TTY skips them.

			Prints MODULE / CURRENT / PLANNED, then asks [y/N] unless
			--confirm or DRY_RUN=1. Commits "chore: update dependencies"
			locally (no push).

