		(none)              → all repos, all releases
		<dir-spec>          → selected repos, all releases
		<version>           → all repos, that version only (SEMVER-shaped)
		<dir-spec> <version>→ selected repos, that version only

	${_CLR_BOLD}--delete${_CLR_RESET}  <dir> <version>
	Remove GitHub Release and tag (local + origin). Confirm with yes.
	--skip-ci is ignored. No-op if neither exists.

	${_CLR_BOLD}CREATE${_CLR_RESET} (default)  <dir> <version> [--skip-ci]
	Tag, push and create a GitHub Release.
	Requires clean tree on master/main, OWNER remote, and CHANGELOG.md with:
		## [<version>] - YYYY-MM-DD
	Notes come from that section. Waits for CI unless --skip-ci
	(Ctrl-C during wait: no tag yet). Same version recreates tag/release.
	Pre-releases (e.g. 1.0.0-rc.1) use gh --prerelease.
	Interactive confirmation (type yes). DRY_RUN supported for create/delete.

